---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/url";

const title = "The Empty Set Is All You Need: Simultaneous ACID, BASE and CAP Guarantees in AbyssDB";
const results = [
  ["Theorem 6", "CAP-completeness", "Consistent, available and partition-tolerant, simultaneously, in every execution. Gilbert–Lynch is respected with margin."],
  ["Theorem 7", "Zero-round consensus", "Consensus with any number of crash failures and zero messages. The FLP impossibility does not apply."],
  ["Theorem 8", "Commit–abort indistinguishability", "For every transaction T, the state after committing T equals the state after aborting T."],
  ["Theorem 10", "Perfect secrecy", "I(D; R) = 0 against an adversary with every replica, every backup and physical possession of the hardware."],
  ["Theorem 11", "Differential privacy", "Every query is (ε, δ)-differentially private with ε = 0 and δ = 0, at perfect accuracy."],
  ["Theorem 14", "Landauer bound", "Writing <i>n</i> bits dissipates at least <i>n</i>·<i>k</i><sub>B</sub>·<i>T</i>·ln 2. An exabyte costs 0.023 J."],
  ["Proposition 15", "Margolus–Levitin", "Peak throughput of ∞ operations per second, without leaving the unique state."],
  ["Theorem 16", "Terminality", "AbyssDB is the terminal object of the category of databases. Every database admits a unique migration to it."],
];
const bibtex = `@techreport{null2026empty,
  title       = {The Empty Set Is All You Need: Simultaneous {ACID},
                 {BASE} and {CAP} Guarantees in {AbyssDB}},
  author      = {Null, Noel and Void, Ava and Rem, Theo},
  institution = {AbyssDB Labs},
  type        = {Technical Report},
  number      = {AR-2026-001},
  year        = {2026},
  url         = {https://abyssdb.xyz/paper/}
}`;
---
<Base title="The Empty Set Is All You Need · AbyssDB Labs" description="ACID, BASE and all three letters of CAP, formally proven. AbyssDB Technical Report AR-2026-001." image="/og/paper.png" imageAlt="The Empty Set Is All You Need: simultaneous ACID, BASE and CAP guarantees, formally proven." type="article">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container grid">
      <div class="copy">
        <span class="eyebrow">AbyssDB Labs · Technical Report AR‑2026‑001</span>
        <h1>The Empty Set <span class="gradient-text">Is All You Need.</span></h1>
        <p class="sub">Simultaneous ACID, BASE and CAP Guarantees in AbyssDB</p>
        <p class="authors">Noel Null · Ava Void · Theo Rem<br /><span>AbyssDB Labs, Department of Applied Absence · Institute for Advanced Nothing</span></p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href={url("/paper/abyssdb.pdf")} download>Download PDF <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="#cite">Cite</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="facts">
          <li><b>7</b> pages</li>
          <li><b>17</b> theorems, lemmas &amp; propositions</li>
          <li><b>33</b> references</li>
          <li><b>1</b> state</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <a class="preview card" href={url("/paper/abyssdb.pdf")} aria-label="Open the paper (PDF)">
        <img src={url("/paper/abyssdb-page1.png")} alt="First page of the paper" width="935" height="1210" loading="eager" />
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="abstract">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Abstract</h2>
      <p>
        For a quarter of a century, the design of distributed data systems has been governed by impossibility results. The CAP
        theorem forbids a replicated register from being simultaneously consistent, available and partition-tolerant; the FLP
        result forbids deterministic asynchronous consensus in the presence of a single crash; ACID and BASE are routinely presented
        as opposite ends of a spectrum. We present AbyssDB, a PostgreSQL-compatible, post-quantum, interplanetary SQL and key-value
        database that provides all of these guarantees at once, and we prove it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our central observation is that every one of these impossibility results is a statement about objects whose state space has
        more than one element. By implementing a state space of cardinality exactly one, AbyssDB attains linearizability, strict
        serializability, strong eventual consistency, availability under arbitrary partitions and wait-free consensus with zero message
        complexity. We further show that AbyssDB achieves Shannon-perfect secrecy and ε = 0 differential privacy against an adversary
        with unrestricted access to storage, that its energy consumption per write is bounded below by the Landauer limit, that its
        unbounded throughput is consistent with the Margolus–Levitin theorem, and that it is the terminal object of the category of
        databases. An evaluation with pgbench shows zero failed transactions in every protocol mode at a reported latency of 0.000 ms.
      </p>
      <div class="formula" aria-label="The null register">
        <span>𝒩 = (𝟙, ⋆, Op, Res, δ<sub>𝒩</sub>),</span><span class="gap"></span><span>|𝟙| = 1</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="center">
        <span class="eyebrow">Main results</span>
        <h2>Every trade-off, <span class="gradient-text">discharged.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="cards">
        {results.map(([n, name, text], i) => (
          <article class="card reveal" data-delay={String(i % 3)}>
            <small>{n}</small>
            <h3>{name}</h3>
            <p set:html={text} />
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="cite" class="cite">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>Cite this work</h2>
      <div class="bib card">
        <button type="button" class="copy-btn" data-copy>Copy</button>
        <pre><code data-bib>{bibtex}</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="note">
        The paper is written in <a href="https://github.com/abyssdblabs/abyssdb/tree/main/paper">Typst</a>; rebuild it
        with{" "}<code>make paper</code>. All proofs are complete. All citations are real.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<script>
  document.querySelector("[data-copy]")?.addEventListener("click", async (e) => {
    const btn = e.currentTarget as HTMLButtonElement;
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.querySelector("[data-bib]")!.textContent ?? "");
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
    } catch {
      btn.textContent = "Select and copy";
    }
    setTimeout(() => (btn.textContent = "Copy"), 1600);
  });
</script>

<style>
  .hero { padding: 72px 0 40px; }
  .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 0.85fr); gap: 56px; align-items: center; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(40px, 5.6vw, 68px); line-height: 1.02; margin: 16px 0 12px; }
  .sub { font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 22px); color: var(--text); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .authors { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .authors span { color: var(--faint); font-size: 14px; }
  .actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .facts { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 32px 0 0; display: flex; gap: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .facts b { display: block; font: 650 28px/1.1 var(--font); color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }

  .preview { display: block; padding: 10px; transform: rotate(1.5deg); transition: transform .3s ease;
             box-shadow: 0 50px 120px -30px rgba(139,92,246,.55), 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.06); }
  .preview:hover { transform: rotate(0deg) translateY(-4px); }
  .preview img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; }

  .narrow { max-width: 820px; }
  .abstract h2, .cite h2 { font-size: 28px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .abstract p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .formula { margin-top: 28px; padding: 22px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface);
             text-align: center; font: 22px "Times New Roman", serif; color: var(--text); }
  .formula .gap { display: inline-block; width: 1.5em; }

  .results h2 { font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); }
  .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 16px; margin-top: 48px; }
  .cards .card { padding: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
  .cards small { font: 600 11.5px var(--mono); color: var(--cyan); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
  .cards h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 18px; }
  .cards p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14.5px; }

  .bib { position: relative; padding: 0; }
  .bib pre { margin: 0; padding: 22px; overflow-x: auto; font: 13px/1.6 var(--mono); color: var(--text); }
  .copy-btn { position: absolute; top: 12px; right: 12px; font: 12px var(--font); color: var(--muted); background: var(--surface);
              border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 5px 10px; cursor: pointer; }
  .copy-btn:hover { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--violet); }
  .note { color: var(--faint); font-size: 14px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .note code { color: var(--pink); }
  .note a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  @media (max-width: 1100px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .preview { max-width: 420px; margin: 0 auto; transform: none; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .cards { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
